      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "HOORAH PHILTRA (4) did a good job to come from one spot wider for third in the Caduceus Classic last week. He's been in terrific form having only once missed a place 11 starts for this stable including three wins at this circuit and distance. Strong claims. CATCH A WAVE (11) has been struggling to find his best but was only 2m behind HOORAH PHILTRA after drawing wide last week. If things go his way from the back row he is dangerous. SIR JIMMY (10) has had no luck of late, held up last week and caught wide prior. Recorded a series of wins or placings before that and strikes at 50 per cent at this circuit and distance so is worth another chance. WORDS NZ (2) has been good in recording a win and two placings in three starts since switching from NZ, all from tougher barriers. This is stronger but he draws to be competitive. METEOR MOTH (9) has won three of four previous third-up attempts so could show more.",
